{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"irongray-unlucky-discus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nInvestigation absurd-zoometric-bobwhite proved that six repeated markerless Jira echo bodies on REB-1567, REB-1931, and REB-2605 account for at least 760 excess COMMENT files / 18,496,834 bytes plus 229,222,450 duplicate body bytes embedded in active and permanently retained snapshots: 247,719,284 logical bytes total. The comment-loop defects are fixed and the workflow converged, but existing artifacts remain reachable. Direct deletion or ad-hoc tracker Git mutation would violate the append-only and merge-as-union safety contracts.\n\n## Plan\n- Enumerate the exact COMMENT events and snapshots attributable to the six proven duplicate body groups, excluding legitimate same-body comments by Jira ID and chronology.\n- Design a reclaim that preserves current reduced state, authorship/audit requirements, merge safety, and causal-stability constraints.\n- Route any tracker rewrite through the supported maintenance/reclaim path with backup refs and dry-run evidence.\n- Specify fresh-clone before/after validation for logical tree, allocated tree, pack bytes, reachability, fsck, and semantic ticket parity.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The target set is deterministic and independently auditable before mutation.\n- [ ] Legitimate comments and current reduced ticket state are proven unchanged.\n- [ ] The procedure complies with tracker-maintenance, backup, and causal-stability requirements.\n- [ ] Expected and observed reclaimed bytes are reported separately for tree, allocation, and pack layers.\n- [ ] Rollback and post-rewrite clone migration steps are explicit.","id":"93c4-2b9f-749a-4243","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["store","reconciler","reclaim","comments"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Design a safe targeted reclaim for duplicated reconciler comments and snapshots"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787520786649330001,"uuid":"c0d7ba39-5fe1-402a-9ea6-e4e8e00f7bf6"}